.TH MAKEPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
makepkg \- construct APKs from staged payloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makepkg
.I PRODUCER
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B makepkg
is the sole APK constructor: it validates the staged payload
(identities, splits, scripts, metadata), embeds file ownership and
account declarations, generates the install/upgrade/deinstall
callers from
.I accounts.d
fragments, and emits unsigned APKs plus the build receipts the
publication gate re-verifies. It never installs anything (see
.BR installpkg (8))
and never publishes (see
.BR sign-apk-repo (8)).
It is normally driven inside
.BR buildpkg (1)
namespaces, not by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the producer name; behavior
comes from the stage manifest plus configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $SAPHIRA_INCOMING_DIR
Where constructed artifacts land for staging.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Constructed and receipted.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, split, identity, or construction failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
makepkg nginx
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR buildpkg (1),
.BR resolvepkg (1),
